# No Regressions After Edits

Every change must leave the rest of the app clean and working. Fix only what the requirement needs, without breaking unrelated behavior.

## Requirements

- Do not introduce runtime crashes, broken flows, or regressions outside the requested edit.
- After code changes, ensure there are **no red marks**: TypeScript errors, ESLint/IDE diagnostics, or broken imports in files you touched (and fix any you caused elsewhere).
- Preserve existing APIs, routes, props, and contracts unless the task explicitly changes them.
- Prefer minimal, targeted diffs. Avoid drive-by refactors that risk unrelated breakage.
- If a change could affect shared paths (auth, layout, API client, schema), verify callers still type-check and behave correctly.
- Do not leave incomplete stubs, unused broken imports, or `any`-hiding that masks real errors.

## Checklist Before Finishing

1. Touched files compile / have no new diagnostics.
2. Related call sites still type-check.
3. Existing features not in scope still work as before.
4. No half-migrated renames or missing exports.

## Examples

```text
# ❌ BAD — fix reports export but break admin layout imports / leave TS errors
# ✅ GOOD — scoped change; diagnostics clean; other pages still work
```
